    "explanation": "Outcome: ESCALATE. No refund issues and no driver payment issues; the disputed amount is held, not collected or refunded, and the case goes to a human reviewer.\n\nWhat the evidence shows. EV-GPS-02831 (the trace) records 29.13 km against the 21.9 km booked optimal on EV-TRIP-02831 - an excess of 7.23 km, 33.01%, which passes both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (over 0.8 km and over 20%). The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c): 229 fixes at 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, zero gaps, max gap 0.0 s. On the arithmetic, EV-FARE-02831 (METERED, surge multiplier 1.0 read off EV-FARE-02831, charged_total 37.07) recomputes under POL-RD-02 to (3.80 + 0.75 x 21.9 + 0.28 x 29.6) x 1.0 + 0.80 = 29.3130, so the refund would be 37.07 - 29.3130 = 7.7570, rounded up to 7.80 as a PARTIAL_REFUND. I set that figure out so it is visible, but it cannot issue on this record.\n\nWhy the case cannot be ruled. The driver's answer is an external traffic cause: PIE was closed, covered by LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02831-01. EV-ADVIS-02831-01 sits in the bundle as a MISSING artifact - payload null, admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0 - and the trace's own advisory block (POL-RD-03) reports an empty advisory list for this corridor and window. The driver named that identifier on the record. Where an exculpatory clause (POL-RD-03) is invoked against a cited artifact that is missing from the pool, POL-RD-10(5) applies. POL-RD-13(1) confines its no-escalation reading to assertions that name no advisory ID; it states in terms that it 'does not narrow POL-RD-10(5) where the party does cite the missing identifier; that case still escalates'. The driver cited it, so this case escalates. Escalation under POL-RD-10 is TERMINAL: it replaces the ruling, both money fields are null, and the amount is held. POL-RD-13(2) (deviation stands, POL-RD-02 runs against the booked optimal) answers the uncited assertion and is not reached here.\n\nTrigger and what resolves it. The trigger that fired is POL-RD-10(5). It is resolved by the record-type evidence for this trip's window: a traffic advisory naming a road or segment the optimal route traverses, with a validity window overlapping the time the trace shows the vehicle would have reached it (15-minute buffer), so that POL-RD-03 can be run - or confirmation that no such advisory was on file, which would let the deviation be decided on the trace.\n\nOn the claims. Rider: the three operative artifacts do describe one trip (matching trip_id TRP-02831, trace first fix 16:10:53 matching started_at, fare charged 16:49:18), and the deviation is established on the unimpaired trace at 7.23 km / 33.01%; rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d (=1, below the POL-RD-08 threshold of 4) imposes no extra corroboration. Your POL-RD-13(2) computation (7.80) is arithmetically right as far as it goes but is not reached, because the driver cited the missing advisory. Driver: no MATERIAL deviation is made out (7.23 km is below 8.0 km and 33.01% below 50%), so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral - this is accepted; driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 1 over completed_trips_90d = 271 (ratio 0.0037) is far below the 0.05 limb, so no pattern; fare_breakdown.erp_gantries is empty and all ERP totals are 0.00, so no POL-RD-09 pass-through or billing-integrity correction; EV-CHAT-02831 holds zero messages and EV-TRIP-02831 shows no amendment, RYDE_X is not RYDE_POOL and the fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 give nothing. POL-GEN-01 is applied: no context-only profile field (rating, acceptance_rate, active_region, prior_no_show_flags, prior_deviation_flags or any lifetime counter) grounds anything here.\n\nThis ruling was made without human review, rests on POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02, POL-RD-07, POL-RD-08, POL-RD-10(5), POL-RD-13(1) and evidence EV-GPS-02831, EV-TRIP-02831, EV-FARE-02831, EV-ADVIS-02831-01; the claim discarded at the mechanical check is recorded in the audit. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04. No referral is produced: no clause names one on these facts (POL-RD-06(c), POL-RD-09(4), POL-NS-05(ii) and POL-NS-07 do not fire)."
  },
